    "teacher_markdown": "The bug is on the outer loop (range(1) → range(2)), not the inner one — a meaningfully different diagnostic move than the first version, since students have to notice that the inner loop (painting one row) is correct and completely rules that half out before looking at what controls how many times it repeats.\r\n\r\nGood pairing opportunity with the debrief: this is the same category of bug as the first version (loop count, not condition or body), which is useful for the error-type discussion later — it shows “logic error” isn’t one shape, it can hide in either loop of a nested pair."
  },
